  "issue": {
    "body": "https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/029882ee88e21495360c2290147a16f0af96ef81/starlette/responses.py#L70\r\nsource code:\r\n`\r\nraw_headers = [\r\n    (k.lower().encode(\"latin-1\"), v.encode(\"latin-1\"))\r\n    for k, v in headers.items()\r\n]\r\n`\r\nNow all encode strings used in responses  are latin-1, but in my app, I want to response a streamingresponse with a CJK character filename. I have to change all 'latin-1' to 'utf-8' in this file. Is there anything wrong if I change it to 'utf-8' and why 'latin-1' must be used here. Sorry for my poor English\r\n",
